NNAAMMEE
       rdma_get_recv_comp - retrieves a completed receive request.

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ##iinncclluuddee <<rrddmmaa//rrddmmaa__vveerrbbss..hh>>

       iinntt rrddmmaa__ggeett__rreeccvv__ccoommpp ((ssttrruucctt rrddmmaa__ccmm__iidd **_i_d,, ssttrruucctt iibbvv__wwcc **_w_c));;

AARRGGUUMMEENNTTSS
       id          A reference to a communication identifier to check for com‐
                   pletions.

       wc          A reference to a work completion structure to fill in.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Retrieves a completed work request for a receive  operation.   Informa‐
       tion  about the completed request is returned through the wc parameter,
       with the wr_id set to the context of the request.  For details  on  the
       work completion structure, see ibv_poll_cq.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       Returns  the  number of returned completions (0 or 1) on success, or -1
       on error.  If an error occurs, errno will be set to indicate the  fail‐
       ure reason.

NNOOTTEESS
       This  calls  polls  the  receive  completion  queue  associated with an
       rdma_cm_id.  If a completion is not found, the call blocks until a  re‐
       quest completes.  This call should only be used on rdma_cm_id's that do
       not share CQs with other rdma_cm_id's, and maintain  separate  CQs  for
       sends and receive completions.

